# No Xcode on the host

Xcode is not installed on this machine and must not be installed or suggested.

Do not run, invoke, or rely on any of the following on the host:

- `xcodebuild`, `xcrun`, `xcode-select`
- `swift`, `swiftc`, or other Apple SDK compilers from a host path
- Opening `.xcodeproj` / `.xcworkspace` or launching the Xcode app
- Installing Xcode, Command Line Tools, or CocoaPods for host use

If something needs compiling or a native toolchain, do it inside a Docker container (`docker exec` into the appropriate project container, or an image that already has the toolchain). Follow the project's container-based development rules — never fall back to Xcode on the Mac.
